Give the page the back gesture, and the shell the items that arrive late.

Two things the shell cannot do for itself.

A back gesture has to reach the page before it reaches the tab. A WebUI or a
site with a <dialog> open -- adding a password in chrome://password-manager,
say -- expects back to close the dialog, and instead the tab went back a page
with the dialog still on screen. Chromium already knows how to ask: a
CloseWatcher on the focused frame, which is what Android's back button
signals. The machinery is inside content and reachable only through the Java
bridge, so WebContents gains the same call without one, and the shell asks
through it before deciding to go back itself.

The other is the context menu. The shell draws it from a list handed over
when the menu opens, so an item that becomes available afterwards is missed
-- and "copy link to highlighted text" is always one of those: it is added
disabled and enabled only once the renderer has generated the text fragment,
a round trip later. It had therefore never once appeared. UpdateMenuItem now
tells the shell, which sends the list again.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch and
ohos-shell-context-menu.patch.

diff --git a/content/public/browser/web_contents.h b/content/public/browser/web_contents.h
--- a/content/public/browser/web_contents.h
+++ b/content/public/browser/web_contents.h
@@ -1222,6 +1222,16 @@
   virtual base::CallbackListSubscription RegisterFocusSelectionBoundsChanged(
       FocusSelectionBoundsChangedCallback callback) = 0;
 
+  // If the focused frame has registered a CloseWatcher -- a <dialog>, a
+  // popover, fullscreen, or a page that called new CloseWatcher() -- gives it
+  // the close signal and returns true. Returns false when there is nothing
+  // listening, and the caller should then do whatever closing means for it.
+  //
+  // This is what a platform's own back gesture has to call first. Android
+  // reaches the same code through RenderFrameHostAndroid; this is the same
+  // thing without a Java bridge in the way.
+  virtual bool SignalCloseWatcherIfActive() = 0;
+
   // Replaces the currently selected word or a word around the cursor.
   virtual void Replace(const std::u16string& word) = 0;
 
